The Shyam Sankar profile does not pass verification: I wrote `verification-edit.json` with status **revise**. It needs one repair pass for three factual errors, and the Type 6 argument scores below the release floor.

## What blocks release

- **A quote he didn't say.** The marriage FAQ says he has referred to "my wife." The only "my wife" in any source is the podcast host, Andrew Bosworth, replying to him. He is still shown to be married: Lonsdale calls him "a husband and a father" on camera, and "my son" and "my daughter" are his.
- **A one-word misquote.** The article prints "we have to sue the army to compete at some point." The captions and my own re-transcription of the audio both give "we *had* to sue."
- **A false statement about the record.** The article says no telling of the family story predates his late-2024 public turn. A September 2023 investor interview already in the evidence file has him saying he grew up "essentially" a child of refugees who "fled violence in Nigeria," raised with gratitude for "the counterfactual." Fixing this helps the page, since it shows the account wasn't invented for the book tour.
- **The type argument.** The page itself says its four observations "lean Six, and none of them settles it," shows no costly choice the Six reading explains better than pay or position, and leaves Types 1 and 3 live. The testing is serious and honest, but that is short of the bar for a standard profile.

