## The fork that's yours

The three factual errors are small edits. The type argument is not a wording problem. A repair can try to strengthen the Six-versus-Eight case from material already sourced: his own rule that a heretic needs "protection from the top," calling Karp his "rabbi… guru… parole officer," and the 2023 telling. If that still doesn't clear the bar on re-verification, the honest outcome is a hold until someone who isn't an ally goes on record about him. I'd let the repair run once and accept the hold if it comes.

## What was checked

- All 23 web sources were re-fetched live today; the SEC filing, court documents, Hudson transcript and Colossus profile match the article.
- YouTube refused fresh caption downloads, so I checked the saved caption tracks and re-transcribed the quoted passages from the saved audio. Two videos had no saved audio and rest on captions alone, including the 2023 interview. None of this is a human listen.
- Bloomberg was read through a third-party reader because the site returned 403.
- A search today found the Pentagon's Minab review still unreleased.
- 154 of 165 claims are supported, 8 are qualified and 3 are unsupported.
- 51 of the editor's 52 fixes are accepted; the one rejected rests on the false "no earlier telling" statement.
- All 17 protected passages are preserved.
- Five minor wording findings are also in the file.

Only `verification-edit.json` was written; nothing was published or edited elsewhere.

